From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thongass000 <tienthong2004@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:45:59 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] imsservice: Carrier data from Samsung's S26

Replace the carrier data, res/raw imsprofile.json, globalsettings.json,
mnomap.json, localconfig.json, rcspolicy.json and res/xml dmconfig.xml,
userconfiguration.xml, with the one of the Galaxy S26 Ultra's
imsservice (m3q, S948BXXS2AZE2): its entries and values only, changed
where this older code needs it.

- Add the 148 carriers it does not know to Mno, taking region and
  country from a known carrier in the same country.
- Keep the keys this code reads; drop values of another JSON type than
  it reads them as, and object values: GlobalSettingsRepoBase.save()
  crashes on them.
- Drop network types ImsProfile$NETWORK_TYPE cannot parse (nr); one
  unknown type makes the loader discard the whole profile.
- Turn the IPsec auth_algo/enc_algo lists into the single keywords
  libsec-ims takes; it puts other values into Security-Client as is and
  the network answers 400 Bad header field.
- Drop the @BLOCKGC flags (no Google Guest Cloud RCS) from mnomap.json's
  carrier names, which Mno would not find otherwise.

tools/imsservice/port_ims_data.py does the conversion;
gen_csc_from_imsswitch.py generates the device tree's customer.xml from
the same release's imsswitch.json.

Assisted-by: LLM
